# Keycloak (see design.md §11). Under Aspire, these should arrive via
# service discovery / injected env vars rather than being hand-copied per
# environment — this file documents the shape for standalone `vite dev`.
#
# VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY is REQUIRED and has no default. Baked in at build time,
# so an image built without it is permanently pointed at nothing: with no value
# the app renders "Sign-in is not configured" instead of redirecting users to
# port 8080 of their own machine, which is what the old localhost default did.
# The value below is the dev realm; production builds must pass their own.
VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=http://localhost:8080/realms/rocketwiki
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=rocketwiki-web
VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/auth/callback
VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173

# GraphQL + SignalR endpoints (see design.md §8). Empty means "same origin"
# (dev proxy / prod nginx both terminate these on the SPA's own origin).
# Browser telemetry also reads these to decide which cross-origin hosts may
# receive a `traceparent` header — see src/telemetry/propagation.ts. The
# SignalR URL is the ONE hub (notifications + presence share it,
# design.md §8); src/realtime/transports.ts builds both transports from it.
VITE_GRAPHQL_URL=/graphql
VITE_SIGNALR_NOTIFICATIONS_URL=/hubs/notifications

# Dev-proxy target — read by vite.config.ts for `npm run dev` ONLY; the
# built SPA never sees it. The dev server proxies /graphql, /hubs
# (WebSocket), /attachments, /avatars, /avatar, /emojis, and /users to this
# origin, which is what makes the same-origin defaults above work without
# the API needing the CORS policy it deliberately doesn't have. Defaults to
# the API's standalone launch profile (http://localhost:5079); under the
# Aspire AppHost the API port is assigned dynamically — read it off the
# Aspire dashboard and set this before `npm run dev` (see DEVELOPING.md).
#VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:5079

# Realtime transports are REAL (SignalR against the hub above) by default.
# Set exactly `true` to run the SPA with in-memory fakes instead — dev
# without a backend only; any other value (or unset) means real. See
# src/realtime/transports.ts.
#VITE_FAKE_REALTIME=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# draw.io / diagrams.net embedded diagram editor. OPTIONAL — and off by
# default, on the same fail-closed rule as telemetry below: with no URL set
# the SPA loads NO external editor and the edit dialog explains how to
# configure one. Editing a diagram posts its full content into whatever page
# this URL serves, so "forgot to configure it" must mean "no editor", never
# "quietly use the public internet service" (design.md §15 — everything
# stays inside the network boundary).
#
# VIEWING never needs this: diagrams are stored inline in the page Markdown
# (```drawio fences, base64 editable SVG) and render as plain data-URI
# images with zero editor involvement.
#
# Production: a self-hosted in-network diagrams.net instance. The AppHost
# defines a dev-only `drawio` container (jgraph/drawio) for this — point at
# its endpoint. Nothing injects this automatically yet (the AppHost doesn't
# run the Vite app; see the OTel note below).
#VITE_DRAWIO_URL=http://localhost:8080
#
# Dev-only opt-in to the PUBLIC editor (the dialog shows a visible
# external-editor warning when it detects this): diagram content is shared
# with diagrams.net while editing. Never for real content.
#VITE_DRAWIO_URL=https://embed.diagrams.net

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser OpenTelemetry (design.md §15). ALL OPTIONAL — and off by default.
#
# With no endpoint set, the tracing SDK is never loaded: no spans, no network
# calls, and the OTel chunk isn't even downloaded. There is deliberately no
# default endpoint, because §15 requires the collector to stay inside the
# network boundary and "forgot to configure it" must fail closed.
#
# What browser spans carry: document load timings, fetch/XHR requests
# (URL path only — query strings and fragments are stripped before export,
# because the SPA puts search text in `?q=` and heading text in `#anchor`),
# and GraphQL operation *names*. Never variables, never request or response
# bodies, never user attribute values.
#
# The AppHost does not currently run the Vite dev server (it's a commented-out
# TODO in src/RocketWiki.AppHost/AppHost.cs), so nothing injects these
# automatically yet — set them by hand for standalone `vite dev`.
#
# Against a local Aspire dashboard, note that its OTLP/**HTTP** endpoint is
# port 18890; 18889 is the gRPC one, which a browser cannot use. A standalone
# dashboard also needs this SPA's origin allowed, or the browser blocks the
# export before it leaves:
#   DASHBOARD__OTLP__CORS__ALLOWEDORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# and when the dashboard has API-key auth on (the default under an AppHost, off
# standalone) the key goes in the `x-otlp-api-key` header below. Once the
# AppHost does run the web app, it configures dashboard CORS for its own
# resources automatically and these become injected rather than hand-set.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base OTLP/HTTP endpoint; `/v1/traces` is appended. Uncomment to enable.
#VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:18890

# Full traces URL, used verbatim, when it isn't `<base>/v1/traces`.
#VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=https://collector.internal/otlp/traces

# Collector auth, `key=value,key2=value2`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !! EVERY `VITE_*` VALUE IS PUBLIC. !!
#
# Vite inlines them into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time. They are not read
# at run time and they are not private: anything set here is served to every
# browser that loads the app and readable by anyone who opens the network tab.
# The value below is therefore only ever appropriate for a local Aspire
# dashboard's throwaway key, which is what this example shows.
#
# A real collector's API key MUST NOT go here. Terminate collector auth
# server-side instead — proxy the OTLP endpoint through the API or an ingress
# that adds the credential — so the secret stays on a server. The same rule
# applies to every other variable in this file: none of them may hold a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=x-otlp-api-key=dev-dashboard-key-only

# Overrides `service.name`, which defaults to `rocketwiki-web`. Worth setting
# on a low-side replica so its traces are distinguishable (replicas:
# design.md §12; telemetry rules: §15).
#VITE_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=rocketwiki-web

# Becomes `service.version`; omitted entirely when unset. Set from the build.
#VITE_APP_VERSION=0.0.0
